{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel lifted up.</b> For from this point onward they needed to be with the children of Israel, to prevail with Elohim and with men, now that they were journeying to a foreign land." "<b>Jacob their father.</b> For in his going to this joy, after which there is no sorrow — since all the troubles that had befallen him had passed — he foresaw what would be decreed for him in the end and in the latter days, as it says: רָנּוּ לְיַעֲקֹב שִׂמְחָה (Jeremiah 31:6)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:51.436182896Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}